; bfsodium SHA_512 : FIPS 180_4
;
; HAND WRITTEN skeleton; The whole of the hash is sha512/hashcore  PASTED; this
; file is the wire interface and nothing else;
;
; IO  in:  len{2} LE  msg{len}
;     out: digest{64}  big endian  as the standard prints it
;
; The length prefix is how the program knows where the message ends; a bfsodium
; primitive never relies on end of input;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x743  sha512/hashcore's frame  pasted at this file's own zero; its
;                 footprint 0:1859 is the whole of this file's tape
;   @0x002:0x003  slen{2}  the count hashcore takes from the wire; this file
;                 fills it and leaves plen at nought  so the entire message
;                 comes off the wire and none of it from the prefix buffer
;   @0x104:0x143  H{8}     the digest  once hashcore has run
;
; hashcore takes its message from a prefix in memory and then from the wire;
; HMAC and HKDF use the prefix  and this uses the wire; that is the whole of the
; difference between them and it is one number;
;
; The SHA_256 file of the same name is this file with three numbers changed  and
; they are the only three: the digest is sixty four bytes rather than thirty two
; the tape is 0:1859 rather than 0:1111  and a hash word is eight bytes;

; read the length into the count hashcore takes from the wire
R2
  ,>,
; ASSERT ptr=3
; ASSERT zero 4:1859
; to hashcore's base  which is where a paste site always stands
L3
; ASSERT ptr=0
@@HASHCORE512@@ 0
; ASSERT ptr=0

; emit
; the digest  big endian  as the standard prints it
; hash word 0  top byte first
R267
  .<.<.<.<.<.<.<.
; hash word 1  top byte first
R15
  .<.<.<.<.<.<.<.
; hash word 2  top byte first
R15
  .<.<.<.<.<.<.<.
; hash word 3  top byte first
R15
  .<.<.<.<.<.<.<.
; hash word 4  top byte first
R15
  .<.<.<.<.<.<.<.
; hash word 5  top byte first
R15
  .<.<.<.<.<.<.<.
; hash word 6  top byte first
R15
  .<.<.<.<.<.<.<.
; hash word 7  top byte first
R15
  .<.<.<.<.<.<.<.
